tonight the clark county school district  board of trustees will talk about the  process of hiring an interim  superintendent now this comes a week  after dr jarrah was fired from his job  kate houston live in studio now to  explain the process of actually filling  that role full time and also what our  next steps might be kate yes dr jarrah  is the first superintendent in ccsd  history to be fired from his position  the process of hiring a superintendent  can take months and even quite a bit of  money local unions want the board to  come together to focus on the task at  hand there have been three different  superintendents over the past 10 years  the search time ranged from two to eight  months consisting of board meetings  parent town halls and recruiters  executives search firms were used for  two out of the three hires jarrah and  dwight jones costing around 50 thousand  dollars each time one superintendent pat  skorkowski was hired locally the  teachers and administrators union says  it's time for some stability and  priorities to shift or the process needs  to be done correctly it needs to be  transparent we need to ensure that  you know the students are again a top  priority staff and the community deserve  that i think that's really important  that we have a superintendent who comes  in and  reestablishes relationships and trusts  with staff as the search starts  administrators union deputy executive  director jeff horn hopes the board will  heavily consider local candidates  the timeline to fill the position full  time remains to be seen tonight the  board will discuss hiring an interim  superintendent both unions want this  process to be done efficiently since dr  jarrah has less than a month left at  ccsd
 

